This is the RAMSES parameter file for the DustyAdvect3D test.

Three-dimensional counterpart of the 1D dustyadvect test. A dust-enriched cube is
advected by an imposed *diagonal* drift velocity, so that all three flux directions of
the TVA solver are exercised at once -- the 1D tests only ever exercise idim=1, which
is how the transverse c_s_face indexing bug in get_dust_courant_dt survived.

The gas is static, so the dust moves only because of the drift. With periodic
boundaries and a constant w, the exact solution is the initial cube translated by w*t,
and the total dust mass is invariant.

&RUN_PARAMS
hydro=.true.
static=.true.
/

&AMR_PARAMS
levelmin=5
levelmax=5
ngridmax=40000
nparttot=1
nexpand=1
boxlen=1.0
/

&BOUNDARY_PARAMS
nboundary=0
/

&INIT_PARAMS
nregion=2
region_type(1)='square'
region_type(2)='square'
x_center=0.5,0.25
y_center=0.5,0.25
z_center=0.5,0.25
length_x=1.0,0.25
length_y=1.0,0.25
length_z=1.0,0.25
exp_region=10,10
d_region=1.0,1.0
u_region=0.0,0.0
v_region=0.0,0.0
w_region=0.0,0.0
p_region=1.0,1.0
var_region(1,1)=0.01d0
var_region(2,1)=0.1d0
/

&OUTPUT_PARAMS
noutput=1
tout=0.1
/

&HYDRO_PARAMS
gamma=1.4
courant_factor=0.8
slope_type=1
riemann='hllc'
/

&REFINE_PARAMS
interpol_var=0
interpol_type=2
/

&CALIMA_PARAMS
dust_tva=.true.
use_w_drift_test=.true.
w_drift_test=1.0,0.5,0.25
tva_wmax_cs=-1.0
dust_composition(1,6) = 1d0
dustbins_per_chemtype=1
asize=0.1d0
sgrain=2.2d0
amin = 3d-2
amax = 1d0
dust_tables_dir='/data80/currodri/test_chicago/rtzdata_for_public_ramses/calima_data/'
/
